  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the previous permission (12th October 2018).\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990.",
    "The hours of work on the site and vehicular movements associated with the development shall only be between 08:00 to 18:00 hours on Mondays to Fridays and 08:00 to 13:00 on Saturdays, and at no time on Sundays, Public or Bank Holidays unless the Council in writing agrees otherwise.\r\rReason: To protect the amenities of the neighbourhood in accordance with policy 29 of Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development shall be maintained in accordance with the Planting Plan (dated May 2009) approved under reference CLC2019/00032. \r\rReason: To ensure the provision, establishment, and maintenance of a reasonable standard of landscape in accordance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan.",
    "All trees that are to be retained shall be protected during the course of construction in accordance with British Standard 5837:1991. \r\rReason: To ensure compliance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan.",
    "The treatment of the materials used on the exterior of the buildings shall be maintained in accordance with the details approved under reference C2000/46444/FUL (as described in the letter dated 10 June 2009). \r\rReason: To safeguard the visual amenity of the area and a high standard of design in accordance with policy 28 of Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The scheme for insulating against noise between the 2nd floor and the new flats shall be maintained in accordance with the details approved under reference C2000/46444/FUL (as described in the letter dated 10 June 2009). \r\rReason: In the interests of the amenities of adjoining residents in accordance with policy 29 of Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The method of refuse storage shall be maintained in accordance with the scheme approved under reference CLC2025/00015. \r\rReason: To ensure that this facility is provided in a manner that integrates with the principal development in accordance with Policies 28 and 29 of the Sutton Local Plan.",
    "The recycling facilities shall be maintained in accordance with the scheme approved under reference CLC2025/00015. \r\rReason: To encourage the collection and recycling of appropriate materials for re-use.",
    "The bicycle storage facilities shall be maintained in accordance with the scheme approved under reference CLC2025/00015. \rReason: To ensure compliance with Policies 28 and 37 of the Sutton Local Plan.",
    "The dormer windows in the western elevation of the west block, the eastern elevation of the east block, and the southern elevation of the south block shall be obscure glazed and fixed shut up to 1.7 metres above floor level and so maintained. \r\rReason: To safeguard the current level of privacy enjoyed by the occupants of adjoining properties in accordance with policy 29 of the sutton local plan 2018."
  ],
